<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Balance Druid DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from Heroics, reputation rewards, and the new 10 and 25-player Raid loot added to Titan Rune Dungeons, as well as the Sidereal and Defiler's Scourgestone vendors.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Balance Druid DPS Pre-Raid Phase 4</h2>With this gear set, you won't be able to meet the crit soft cap. However, you can and should aim to meet the required Hit rating. If you are fully talented into <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33596/balance-of-power">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_balanceofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Balance of Power</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33602/improved-faerie-fire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Improved Faerie Fire</span></a>, you only need 10% Hit from gear (263 rating) to reach the hit cap requirement for a boss fight. Further, if you have a Draenei in your party, only 9% Hit is required from gear (236 rating).<br/>
<br/>Crit was already a valuable stat for Balance Druids but just got even better thanks to the reworked <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=24858/moonkin-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_forceofnature.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Moonkin Form</span></a> where you now regenerate 2% mana when you crit. This vastly improves our mana in Wrath of the Lich King. In early phases, mana can be a bit of a restraint until you get more stats on gear, which means early sources of crit can go a long way not only for damage but for mana regen.<br/>
<br/>The set below is just an example of pre-raid BiS gear. There are a number of variations in order to get ready for raiding, especially depending on which professions you have. This set is also much more than you will need to enter current phase content and will leave you more than ready to participate in the Icecrown Citadel raid on 10 or 25 player versions, though, you may need some more gear to face the heroic versions. This set assumes you have access to Engineering and Tailoring.<br/>
<br/>For more information on individual gear slots or crafted items, read the sections below.<br/>
<br/>
